\f2\page\pard\sl276\slmult1\i\f4\fs36 Concerning the Proper \par
of the Church Year\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl204\slmult1\par
\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 The Proper of the Church Year includes the appointed Collects; the\par
Proper Prefaces, directions for which are to be found in the pages\par
following; and the appointed Psalms and Lessons, which appear in tables\par
beginning on page 889.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 The Proper appointed for the Sunday is also used at celebrations of the\par
Eucharist on the weekdays following, unless otherwise ordered for Holy\par
Days and Various Occasions.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 The Proper to be used on each of the Sundays after Pentecost (except for\par
Trinity Sunday) is determined by the calendar date of that Sunday. Thus,\par
in any year, the Proper for the Sunday after Trinity Sunday (the Second \par
Sunday after Pentecost) is the numbered Proper (number 3 through\par
number 8), the calendar date of which falls on that Sunday, or is closest\par
to it, whether before or after. Thereafter, the Propers are used \par
consecutively. For example, if the Sunday after Trinity Sunday is May 26,\par
the sequence begins with Proper 3 (Propers 1 and 2 being used on the\par
weekdays of Pentecost and Trinity weeks). If the Sunday after Trinity \par
Sunday is June 13, the sequence begins with Proper 6 (Propers 1 through\par
3 being omitted that year, and Propers 4 and 5 being used in Pentecost \par
and Trinity weeks). See also the Table on pages 884-885.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 The Collect appointed for any Sunday or other Feast may be used at the\par
evening service of the day before.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Directions concerning the Common of Saints and services for Various\par
Occasions are on pages 195, 199, 246 and 251.\par
\par
\f2\page\f4\fs44 Collects:  Traditional\fs24\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\b First Sunday of Advent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, give us grace that we may cast away the \par
works of darkness, and put upon us the armor of light, now \par
in the time of this mortal life in which thy Son Jesus Christ \par
came to visit us in great humility; that in the last day, when \par
he shall come again in his glorious majesty to judge both the \par
quick and the dead, we may rise to the life immortal; through \par
him who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Ghost, \par
one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Advent\i0\par
\par
\b Second Sunday of Advent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Merciful God, who sent thy messengers the prophets to \par
preach repentance and prepare the way for our salvation: \par
Give us grace to heed their warnings and forsake our sins, \par
that we may greet with joy the coming of Jesus Christ our \par
Redeemer; who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy\par
Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Advent\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 Third Sunday of Advent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Stir up thy power, O Lord, and with great might come \par
among us; and, because we are sorely hindered by our sins, \par
let thy bountiful grace and mercy speedily help and deliver \par
us; through Jesus Christ our Lord, to whom, with thee and \par
the Holy Ghost, be honor and glory, world without end.  \par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Advent\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 Wednesday, Friday, and Saturday of this week are the traditional winter \par
Ember Days\i0\fs24 .\par
\par
\b Fourth Sunday of Advent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 We beseech thee, Almighty God, to purify our consciences by \par
thy daily visitation, that when thy Son our Lord cometh he\par
may find in us a mansion prepared for himself; through the\par
same Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for \par
ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Advent\i0\par
\par
\b The Nativity of Our Lord: Christmas Day\b0   \i\fs20 December 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who makest us glad with the yearly remembrance of \par
the birth of thy only Son Jesus Christ:  Grant that as we \par
joyfully receive him for our Redeemer, so we may with sure \par
confidence behold him when he shall come to be our Judge; \par
who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Ghost, one \par
God, world without end.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or the following\i0\fs24\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 O God, who hast caused this holy night to shine with the \par
illumination of the true Light:  Grant us, we beseech thee,\par
that as we have known the mystery of that Light upon earth, \par
so may we also perfectly enjoy him in heaven; where with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit he liveth and reigneth, one God, in \par
glory everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who hast given us thy only-begotten Son to\par
take our nature upon him and as at this time to be born of a\par
pure virgin:  Grant that we, being regenerate and made thy \par
children by adoption and grace, may daily be renewed by thy \par
Holy Spirit; through the same our Lord Jesus Christ, who\par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the same Spirit ever, one\par
God, world without end.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Incarnation\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 The Collect immediately preceding and any of the sets of Proper Lessons \par
for Christmas Day serve for any weekdays between Holy Innocents' Day \par
and the First Sunday after Christmas Day.\fs24\par
\i0\par
\b First Sunday after Christmas Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 This Sunday takes precedence over the three Holy Days which follow \par
Christmas Day.  As necessary, the observance of one, two, or all three \par
of them, is postponed one day.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who hast poured upon us the new light of\par
thine incarnate Word:  Grant that the same light, enkindled in \par
our hearts, may shine forth in our lives; through the same\par
Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee, in \par
the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Incarnation\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 The Holy Name\b0    \i\fs20 January 1\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Eternal Father, who didst give to thine incarnate Son the holy \par
name of Jesus to be the sign of our salvation:  Plant in every \par
heart, we beseech thee, the love of him who is the Savior of \par
the world, even our Lord Jesus Christ; who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, in glory \par
everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Incarnation\i0\par
\par
\b Second Sunday after Christmas Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who didst wonderfully create, and yet more \par
wonderfully restore, the dignity of human nature:  Grant \par
that we may share the divine life of him who humbled \par
himself to share our humanity, thy Son Jesus Christ; who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Incarnation\i0\par
\par
\b The Epiphany\b0    \i\fs20 January 6\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who by the leading of a star didst manifest thy only-\par
begotten Son to the peoples of the earth:  Lead us, who know \par
thee now by faith, to thy presence, where we may behold thy \par
glory face to face; through the same Jesus Christ our Lord, \par
who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one \par
God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\par
\i\fs20 The preceding Collect, with the Psalm and Lessons for the Epiphany, or \par
those for the Second Sunday after Christmas Day, serves for weekdays \par
between the Epiphany and the following Sunday. The Preface of the \par
Epiphany is used.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 First Sunday after the Epiphany: The Baptism of our Lord\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Father in heaven, who at the baptism of Jesus in the River\par
Jordan didst proclaim him thy beloved Son and anoint him\par
with the Holy Spirit: Grant that all who are baptized into his \par
Name may keep the covenant they have made, and boldly\par
confess him as Lord and Savior; who with thee and the same\par
Spirit liveth and reigneth, one God, in glory everlasting. \par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\par
\b Second Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, whose Son our Savior Jesus Christ is the light \par
of the world: Grant that thy people, illumined by thy Word \par
and Sacraments, may shine with the radiance of Christ's\par
glory, that he may be known, worshiped, and obeyed to the \par
ends of the earth; through the same Jesus Christ our Lord, \par
who with thee and the Holy Spirit liveth and reigneth, one \par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Third Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Give us grace, O Lord, to answer readily the call of our \par
Savior Jesus Christ and proclaim to all people the Good \par
News of his salvation, that we and all the whole world may \par
perceive the glory of his marvelous works; who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and \par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 Fourth Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, who dost govern all things in \par
heaven and earth: Mercifully hear the supplications of thy people, and in our time grant us thy peace; through Jesus\par
Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Fifth Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Set us free, O God, from the bondage of our sins and give us,\par
we beseech thee, the liberty of that abundant life which thou\par
hast manifested to us in thy Son our Savior Jesus Christ; who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Sixth Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, the strength of all those who put their trust in thee: \par
Mercifully accept our prayers; and because through the \par
weakness of our mortal nature, we can do no good thing\par
without thee, grant us the help of thy grace, that in keeping \par
thy commandments we may please thee both in will and deed; \par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Seventh Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Lord, who hast taught us that all our doings without\par
charity are nothing worth: Send thy Holy Ghost and pour \par
\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 into our hearts that most excellent gift of charity, the very\par
bond of peace and of all virtues, without which whosoever \par
liveth is counted dead before thee. Grant this for thine only \par
Son Jesus Christ\rquote s sake, who liveth and reigneth with thee \par
and the same Holy Ghost, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Eighth Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O most loving Father, who willest us to give thanks for all \par
things, to dread nothing but the loss of thee, and to cast all \par
our care on thee who carest for us:  Preserve us from faithless \par
fears and worldly anxieties, and grant that no clouds of this \par
mortal life may hide from us the light of that love which is \par
immortal, and which thou hast manifested unto us in thy Son \par
Jesus Christ our Lord; who liveth and reigneth with thee, in \par
the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany, or of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Last Sunday after the Epiphany\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 This Proper is always used on the Sunday before Ash Wednesday\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who before the passion of thy only-begotten Son \par
didst reveal his glory upon the holy mount:  Grant unto us \par
that we, beholding by faith the light of his countenance, may \par
be strengthened to bear our cross, and be changed into his \par
likeness from glory to glory; through the same Jesus Christ \par
our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy \par
Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 Ash Wednesday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 The Proper Liturgy for this day is on page 264.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, who hatest nothing that thou\par
hast made and dost forgive the sins of all those who are \par
penitent:  Create and make in us new and contrite hearts, that \par
we, worthily lamenting our sins and acknowledging our \par
wretchedness, may obtain of thee, the God of all mercy, \par
perfect remission and forgiveness; through Jesus Christ our \par
Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Lent\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 This Collect, with the corresponding Psalm and Lessons, serves for \par
the weekdays which follow, except as otherwise appointed.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\b First Sunday in Lent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, whose blessed Son was led by the Spirit to be\par
tempted of Satan: Make speed to help thy servants who are\par
assaulted by manifold temptations; and, as thou knowest\par
their several infirmities, let each one find thee mighty to save; through Jesus Christ thy Son our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for \par
ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Lent\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 Wednesday, Friday, and Saturday of this week are the traditional spring \par
Ember Days.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\b Second Sunday in Lent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, whose glory it is always to have mercy:  Be gracious\par
to all who have gone astray from thy ways, and bring them\par
again with penitent hearts and steadfast faith to embrace and\par
hold fast the unchangeable truth of thy Word, Jesus Christ\par
\f2\page\f4 thy Son; who with thee and the Holy Spirit liveth and \par
reigneth, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Lent\par
\i0\par
\b Third Sunday in Lent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who seest that we have no power of ourselves\par
to help ourselves:  Keep us both outwardly in our bodies and \par
inwardly in our souls, that we may be defended from all \par
adversities which may happen to the body, and from all evil \par
thoughts which may assault and hurt the soul; through Jesus \par
Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the \par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Lent\i0\par
\par
\b Fourth Sunday in Lent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Gracious Father, whose blessed Son Jesus Christ came down \par
from heaven to be the true bread which giveth life to the \par
world:  Evermore give us this bread, that he may live in us, \par
and we in him; who liveth and reigneth with thee and the \par
Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Lent\i0\par
\par
\b Fifth Sunday in Lent\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, who alone canst order the unruly wills and \par
affections of sinful men:  Grant unto thy people that they may\par
love the thing which thou commandest, and desire that \par
which thou dost promise; that so, among the sundry and \par
manifold changes of the world, our hearts may surely there \par
be fixed where true joys are to be found; through Jesus \par
Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the \par
Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Lent\i0\par
\par
\b\par
\b0\f2\page\b\f4 Sunday of the Passion:  Palm Sunday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 The Proper Liturgy for this day is on page 270.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, who, of thy tender love \par
towards mankind, hast sent thy Son our Savior Jesus Christ \par
to take upon him our flesh, and to suffer death upon the \par
cross, that all mankind should follow the example of his \par
great humility:  Mercifully grant that we may both follow the\par
example of his patience, and also be made partakers of his\par
resurrection; through the same Jesus Christ our Lord, who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Holy Week\i0\par
\par
\b Monday in Holy Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, whose most dear Son went not up to joy but\par
first he suffered pain, and entered not into glory before he \par
was crucified:  Mercifully grant that we, walking in the way \par
of the cross, may find it none other than the way of life and \par
peace; through the same thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Holy Week\par
\i0\par
\b Tuesday in Holy Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who by the passion of thy blessed Son didst make an \par
instrument of shameful death to be unto us the means of life: \par
Grant us so to glory in the cross of Christ, that we may gladly \par
suffer shame and loss for the sake of thy Son our Savior Jesus \par
Christ; who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Holy Week\i0\par
\par
\par
\b\par
\b0\f2\page\b\f4 Wednesday in Holy Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Lord God, whose blessed Son our Savior gave his back to\par
the smiters and hid not his face from shame:  Grant us grace \par
to take joyfully the sufferings of the present time, in full\par
assurance of the glory that shall be revealed; through the same\par
thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Holy Week\par
\i0\par
\b Maundy Thursday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 The Proper Liturgy for this day is on page 274.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty Father, whose dear Son, on the night before he \par
suffered, did institute the Sacrament of his Body and Blood: Mercifully grant that we may thankfully receive the same in remembrance of him who in these holy mysteries giveth us a\par
pledge of life eternal, the same thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord; \par
who now liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, \par
ever one God, world without end.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Holy Week\i0\par
\par
\b Good Friday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 The Proper Liturgy for this day is on page 276.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, we beseech thee graciously to behold this thy \par
family, for which our Lord Jesus Christ was contented to be\par
betrayed, and given up into the hands of sinners, and to suffer \par
death upon the cross; who now liveth and reigneth with thee \par
and the Holy Ghost ever, one God, world without end. \i Amen\i0 .\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 Holy Saturday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 The Proper Liturgy for this day is on page 283.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, Creator of heaven and earth:  Grant that, as the\par
crucified body of thy dear Son was laid in the tomb and\par
rested on this holy Sabbath, so we may await with him the\par
coming of the third day, and rise with him to newness of life;\par
who now liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit,\par
one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\par
\b Easter Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 The Liturgy of the Easter Vigil is on page 285.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who for our redemption didst give thine \par
only-begotten Son to the death of the cross, and by his \par
glorious resurrection hast delivered us from the power of \par
our enemy:  Grant us so to die daily to sin, that we may \par
evermore live with him in the joy of his resurrection; through \par
the same thy Son Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth \par
with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who didst make this most holy night to shine with \par
the glory of the Lord's resurrection:  Stir up in thy Church \par
that Spirit of adoption which is given to us in Baptism, that \par
we, being renewed both in body and mind, may worship thee \par
in sincerity and truth; through the same Jesus Christ our \par
Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the \par
same Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who through thine only-begotten Son Jesus \par
Christ hast overcome death and opened unto us the gate of \par
everlasting life:  Grant that we, who celebrate with joy the \par
\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 day of the Lord's resurrection, may be raised from the death \par
of sin by thy life-giving Spirit; through the same Jesus Christ \par
our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the same\par
Spirit ever, one God, world without end.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\i0\par
\par
\b Monday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant, we beseech thee, Almighty God, that we who celebrate \par
with reverence the Paschal feast may be found worthy to \par
attain to everlasting joys; through Jesus Christ our Lord, \par
who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one \par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\i0\par
\par
\b Tuesday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who by the glorious resurrection of thy Son Jesus \par
Christ destroyed death and brought life and immortality to \par
light:  Grant that we, who have been raised with him, may \par
abide in his presence and rejoice in the hope of eternal glory; \par
through the same Jesus Christ our Lord, to whom, with thee \par
and the  Holy Spirit, be dominion and praise for ever and \par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\i0\par
\par
\b Wednesday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, whose blessed Son did manifest himself to his disciples \par
in the breaking of bread:  Open, we pray thee, the eyes of our \par
faith, that we may behold him in all his redeeming work; \par
through the same thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth\par
and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one \par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\i0\par
\par
\b\par
\b0\f2\page\b\f4 Thursday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, who in the Paschal mystery \par
hast established the new covenant of reconciliation:  Grant \par
that all who have been reborn into the fellowship of Christ's \par
Body may show forth in their lives what they profess by their \par
faith; through the same Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth \par
and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever \par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\i0\par
\par
\b Friday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty Father, who hast given thine only Son to die for our \par
sins and to rise again for our justification: Grant us so to put \par
away the leaven of malice and wickedness, that we may always\par
serve thee in pureness of living and truth; through the same\par
thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\i0\par
\par
\b Saturday in Easter Week\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 We thank thee, heavenly Father, for that thou hast delivered\par
us from the dominion of sin and death and hast brought us\par
into the kingdom of thy Son; and we pray thee that, as by his\par
death he hath recalled us to life, so by his love he may raise us \par
to joys eternal; who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the\par
unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\i0\par
\par
\b Second Sunday of Easter\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, who in the Paschal mystery \par
hast established the new covenant of reconciliation:  Grant \par
that all who have been reborn into the fellowship of Christ\rquote s \par
\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 Body may show forth in their lives what they profess by their \par
faith; through the same Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth \par
and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever \par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\i0\par
\par
\b Third Sunday of Easter\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, whose blessed Son did manifest himself to his disciples \par
in the breaking of bread:  Open, we pray thee, the eyes of our \par
faith, that we may behold him in all his redeeming work; \par
through the same thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth\par
and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one \par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\i0\par
\par
\b Fourth Sunday of Easter\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\b0\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, whose Son Jesus is the good shepherd of thy people: \par
Grant that when we hear his voice we may know him who\par
calleth us each by name, and follow where he doth lead; \par
who, with thee and the Holy Spirit, liveth and reigneth, one \par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\i0\par
\par
\b Fifth Sunday of Easter\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, whom truly to know is everlasting life:  \par
Grant us so perfectly to know thy Son Jesus Christ to be the \par
way, the truth, and the life, that we may steadfastly follow \par
his steps in the way that leadeth to eternal life; through the\par
same thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth \par
with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever \par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\i0\par
\par
\b\par
\b0\f2\page\b\f4 Sixth Sunday of Easter\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who hast prepared for those who love thee such \par
good things as pass man's understanding:  Pour into our \par
hearts such love toward thee, that we, loving thee in all \par
things and above all things, may obtain thy promises, which \par
exceed all that we can desire; through Jesus Christ our Lord, \par
who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one \par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Easter\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 Monday, Tuesday, and Wednesday of this week are the traditional \par
Rogation Days.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\b Ascension Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, whose blessed Son our Savior Jesus Christ \par
ascended far above all heavens that he might fill all things: \par
Mercifully give us faith to perceive that, according to his \par
promise, he abideth with his Church on earth, even unto the \par
end of the ages; through the same Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, in \par
glory everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant, we beseech thee, Almighty God, that like as we do\par
believe thy only-begotten Son our Lord Jesus Christ to have \par
ascended into the heavens, so we may also in heart and mind \par
thither ascend, and with him continually dwell; who liveth \par
and reigneth with thee and the Holy Ghost, one God, world\par
without end.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Ascension\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 Either of the preceding Collects, with the proper Psalm and Lessons for \par
Ascension Day, serves for the following weekdays, except as otherwise \par
appointed.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\par
\f2\fs20\page\b\f4\fs24 Seventh Sunday of Easter: The Sunday after Ascension Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, the King of glory, who hast exalted thine only Son\par
Jesus Christ with great triumph unto thy kingdom in heaven: \par
We beseech thee, leave us not comfortless, but send to us \par
thine Holy Ghost to comfort us, and exalt us unto the same\par
place whither our Savior Christ is gone before; who liveth \par
and reigneth with thee and the same Holy Ghost, one God, \par
world without end.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Ascension\i0\par
\par
\b The Day of Pentecost: Whitsunday\b0\par
\par
\i\fs20 When a Vigil of Pentecost is observed, it begins with the Service of Light, \par
page 109 (substituting, if desired, the Gloria in excelsis for the Phos \par
hilaron), and continues with the Salutation and Collect of the Day. Three \par
or more of the appointed Lessons are read before the Gospel, each \par
followed by a Psalm, Canticle, or hymn. Holy Baptism or Confirmation\par
(beginning with the Presentation of the Candidates), or the Renewal of\par
Baptismal Vows, page 292, follows the Sermon.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who on this day didst open the way of eternal \par
life to every race and nation by the promised gift of thy Holy \par
Spirit:  Shed abroad this gift throughout the world by the \par
preaching of the Gospel, that it may reach to the ends of the \par
earth; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth \par
with thee, in the unity of the same Spirit, one God, for ever \par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who on this day didst teach the hearts of thy faithful \par
people by sending to them the light of thy Holy Spirit: Grant \par
us by the same Spirit to have a right judgment in all things, and evermore to rejoice in his holy comfort; through the merits of Christ Jesus our Savior, who liveth and reigneth with thee, in \par
the unity of the same Spirit, one God, world without end. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Pentecost\par
\i0\f2\page\i\f4\fs20 On the weekdays which follow, the numbered Proper which corresponds \par
most closely to the date of Pentecost in that year is used. See page 158.\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 Wednesday, Friday, and Saturday of this week are the traditional summer \par
Ember Days.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\b First Sunday after Pentecost:  Trinity Sunday\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, who hast given unto us\par
thy servants grace, by the confession of a true faith, to\par
acknowledge the glory of the eternal Trinity, and in the power \par
of the Divine Majesty to worship the Unity: We beseech thee\par
that thou wouldest keep us steadfast in this faith and worship, \par
and bring us at last to see thee in thy one and eternal glory, \par
O Father; who with the Son and the Holy Spirit livest and \par
reignest, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Trinity Sunday\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 On the weekdays which follow, the numbered Proper which corresponds \par
most closely to the date of Trinity Sunday in that year is used.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\par
\fs36 The Season after Pentecost\fs24\par
\par
\par
\i\fs20 Directions for the use of the Propers which follow are on page 158.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\b Proper 1\b0   \i\fs20 Week of the Sunday closest to May 11\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Remember, O Lord, what thou hast wrought in us and not\par
what we deserve; and, as thou hast called us to thy service, \par
make us worthy of our calling; through Jesus Christ our \par
\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 No Proper Preface is used.\fs24\par
\i0\par
\b Proper 2\b0   \i\fs20 Week of the Sunday closest to May 18\i0\fs24\par
\par
O Almighty and most merciful God, of thy bountiful goodness \par
keep us, we beseech thee, from all things that may hurt us, \par
that we, being ready both in body and soul, may with free \par
hearts accomplish those things which belong to thy purpose; \par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 No Proper Preface is used.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\b Proper 3\b0   \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to May 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant, O Lord, we beseech thee, that the course of this world \par
may be peaceably governed by thy providence, and that thy \par
Church may joyfully serve thee in confidence and serenity; \par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 4\b0   \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to June 1\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, whose never-failing providence ordereth all things \par
both in heaven and earth:  We humbly beseech thee to put \par
away from us all hurtful things, and to give us those things \par
which are profitable for us; through Jesus Christ our Lord, \par
who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one \par
God, for ever and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 Proper 5\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to June 8\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, from whom all good doth come:  Grant that by thy \par
inspiration we may think those things that are right, and by \par
thy merciful guiding may perform the same; through Jesus \par
Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the \par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 6\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to June 15\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Keep, O Lord, we beseech thee, thy household the Church in \par
thy steadfast faith and love, that by the help of thy grace we\par
may proclaim thy truth with boldness, and minister thy\par
justice with compassion; for the sake of our Savior Jesus \par
Christ, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\fs24\par
\par
\b Proper 7\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to June 22\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Lord, we beseech thee, make us to have a perpetual fear\par
and love of thy holy Name, for thou never failest to help and \par
govern those whom thou hast set upon the sure foundation \par
of thy loving-kindness; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 8\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to June 29\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, who hast built thy Church upon the\par
foundation of the apostles and prophets, Jesus Christ himself \par
being the chief cornerstone:  Grant us so to be joined together \par
in unity of spirit by their doctrine, that we may be made an\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 holy temple acceptable unto thee; through the same Jesus \par
Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the \par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 9\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to July 6\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who hast taught us to keep all thy commandments\par
by loving thee and our neighbor: Grant us the grace of thy \par
Holy Spirit, that we may be devoted to thee with our whole\par
heart, and united to one another with pure affection; \par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the same Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 10\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to July 13\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Lord, we beseech thee mercifully to receive the prayers of \par
thy people who call upon thee, and grant that they may both\par
perceive and know what things they ought to do, and also \par
may have grace and power faithfully to fulfill the same; \par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 11\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to July 20\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, the fountain of all wisdom, who knowest our \par
necessities before we ask and our ignorance in asking:  Have \par
compassion, we beseech thee, upon our infirmities, and those\par
things which for our unworthiness we dare not, and for our \par
blindness we cannot ask, mercifully give us for the worthiness \par
of thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b\par
\b0\f2\page\b\f4 Proper 12\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to July 27\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, the protector of all that trust in thee, without whom \par
nothing is strong, nothing is holy:  Increase and multiply \par
upon us thy mercy; that, thou being our ruler and guide, we \par
may so pass through things temporal, that we finally lose not \par
the things eternal; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth \par
and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever \par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface to the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 13\b0    \i The Sunday closest to August 3\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Lord, we beseech thee, let thy continual pity cleanse and \par
defend thy Church, and, because it cannot continue in safety \par
without thy succor, preserve it evermore by thy help and\par
goodness; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and \par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 14\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to August 10\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant to us, Lord, we beseech thee, the spirit to think and do \par
always such things as are right, that we, who cannot exist \par
without thee, may by thee be enabled to live according to thy \par
will; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth \par
with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 15\b0    The Sunday closest to August 17\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who hast given thy only Son to be unto us \par
both a sacrifice for sin and also an example of godly life:  \par
Give us grace that we may always most thankfully receive\par
that his inestimable benefit, and also daily endeavor\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 ourselves to follow the blessed steps of his most holy life;\par
through the same thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one \par
God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 16\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to August 24\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant, we beseech thee, merciful God, that thy Church, \par
being gathered together in unity by thy Holy Spirit, may \par
manifest thy power among all peoples, to the glory of thy \par
Name; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the same Spirit, one God, world\par
without end.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 17\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to August 31\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Lord of all power and might, who art the author and giver of \par
all good things: Graft in our hearts the love of thy Name, \par
increase in us true religion, nourish us with all goodness, \par
and bring forth in us the fruit of good works; through Jesus \par
Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the \par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 18\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to September 7\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant us, O Lord, we pray thee, to trust in thee with all our \par
heart; seeing that, as thou dost alway resist the proud who \par
confide in their own strength, so thou dost not forsake those \par
who make their boast of thy mercy; through Jesus Christ our \par
Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b\par
\b0\f2\page\b\f4 Proper 19\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to September 14\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, forasmuch as without thee we are not able to please \par
thee, mercifully grant that thy Holy Spirit may in all things \par
direct and rule our hearts; through Jesus Christ our Lord, \par
who with thee and the same Spirit liveth and reigneth, one \par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 The Wednesday, Friday, and Saturday after September 14 are the \par
traditional autumnal Ember Days.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\b Proper 20\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to September 21\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant us, O Lord, not to mind earthly things, but to love \par
things heavenly; and even now, while we are placed among \par
things that are passing away, to cleave to those that shall \par
abide; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever \par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 21\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to September 28\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who declarest thy almighty power chiefly in showing\par
mercy and pity:  Mercifully grant unto us such a measure of \par
thy grace, that we, running to obtain thy promises, may be\par
made partakers of thy heavenly treasure; through Jesus Christ \par
our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy \par
Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 22\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to October 5\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, who art always more ready to \par
hear than we to pray, and art wont to give more than either \par
we desire or deserve:  Pour down upon us the abundance of \par
\par
\f2\page\f4 thy mercy, forgiving us those things whereof our conscience \par
is afraid, and giving us those good things which we are not \par
worthy to ask, but through the merits and mediation of Jesus \par
Christ thy Son our Lord; who liveth and reigneth with thee \par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 23\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to October 12\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Lord, we pray thee that thy grace may always precede and\par
follow us, and make us continually to be given to all good \par
works; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and \par
for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 24\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to October 19\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, who in Christ hast revealed \par
thy glory among the nations:  Preserve the works of thy \par
mercy, that thy Church throughout the world may persevere \par
with steadfast faith in the confession of thy Name; through \par
the same Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord\rquote s Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 25\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to October 26\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, give unto us the increase of\par
faith, hope, and charity; and, that we may obtain that which\par
thou dost promise, make us to love that which thou dost\par
command; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever \par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b\par
\b0\f2\page\b\f4 Proper 26\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to November 2\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and merciful God, of whose only gift it cometh that \par
thy faithful people do unto thee true and laudable service:  \par
Grant, we beseech thee, that we may run without stumbling \par
to obtain thy heavenly promises; through Jesus Christ our \par
Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 27\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to November 9\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, whose blessed Son was manifested that he might \par
destroy the works of the devil and make us the children of \par
God and heirs of eternal life:  Grant us, we beseech thee, that, \par
having this hope, we may purify ourselves even as he is pure; \par
that, when he shall appear again with power and great glory, \par
we may be made like unto him in his eternal and glorious \par
kingdom; where with thee, O Father, and thee, O Holy Ghost,\par
he liveth and reigneth ever, one God, world without end.  \i\par
Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\b Proper 28\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to November 16\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Blessed Lord, who hast caused all holy Scriptures to be \par
written for our learning:  Grant that we may in such wise\par
hear them, read, mark, learn, and inwardly digest them; that,\par
by patience and comfort of thy holy Word, we may embrace \par
and ever hold fast the blessed hope of everlasting life, which \par
thou hast given us in our Savior Jesus Christ; who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and \par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 Proper 29\b0    \i\fs20 The Sunday closest to November 23\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, whose will it is to restore all \par
things in thy well-beloved Son, the King of kings and Lord of \par
lords:  Mercifully grant that the peoples of the earth, divided \par
and enslaved by sin, may be freed and brought together\par
under his most gracious rule; who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Lord's Day, or of Baptism\i0\par
\par
\par
\par
\fs36 Holy Days\fs24  \par
\par
\par
\b Saint Andrew\b0    \i\fs20 November 30\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who didst give such grace to thine apostle \par
Andrew that he readily obeyed the call of thy Son Jesus \par
Christ, and brought his brother with him: Give unto us, who \par
are called by thy Word, grace to follow him without delay, \par
and to bring those near to us into his gracious presence; who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Apostles\par
\i0\par
\b Saint Thomas\b0    \i\fs20 December 21\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Everliving God, who didst strengthen thine apostle Thomas \par
with sure and certain faith in thy Son's resurrection: Grant us \par
so perfectly and without doubt to believe in Jesus Christ, our \par
Lord and our God, that our faith may never be found wanting \par
in thy sight; through him who liveth and reigneth with thee \par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\b\par
\b0\f2\page\b\f4 Saint Stephen\b0    \i\fs20 December 26\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 We give thee thanks, O Lord of glory, for the example of the\par
first martyr Stephen, who looked up to heaven and prayed \par
for his persecutors to thy Son Jesus Christ, who standeth at \par
thy right hand; where he liveth and reigneth with thee and \par
the Holy Spirit, one God, in glory everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\par
Preface of the Incarnation\i0\par
\par
\b Saint John\b0    \i\fs20 December 27\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Shed upon thy Church, we beseech thee, O Lord, the \par
brightness of thy light; that we, being illumined by the \par
teaching of thine apostle and evangelist John, may so walk \par
in the light of thy truth, that we may at length attain to the \par
fullness of life everlasting; through Jesus Christ our Lord, \par
who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one\par
God, for ever and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Incarnation\i0\par
\par
\b The Holy Innocents\b0    \i\fs20 December 28\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 We remember this day, O God, the slaughter of the holy\par
innocents of Bethlehem by the order of King Herod. Receive, \par
we beseech thee, into the arms of thy mercy all innocent \par
victims; and by thy great might frustrate the designs of evil \par
tyrants and establish thy rule of justice, love, and peace; \par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and \par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Incarnation\par
\i0\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 Confession of Saint Peter\b0    \i\fs20 January 18\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty Father, who didst inspire Simon Peter, first among \par
the apostles, to confess Jesus as Messiah and Son of the living \par
God: Keep thy Church steadfast upon the rock of this faith, \par
that in unity and peace we may proclaim the one truth and \par
follow the one Lord, our Savior Jesus Christ; who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for \par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\b Conversion of Saint Paul\b0    \i\fs20 January 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who, by the preaching of thine apostle Paul, hast\par
caused the light of the Gospel to shine throughout the world:  \par
Grant, we beseech thee, that we, having his wonderful \par
conversion in remembrance, may show forth our thankfulness \par
unto thee for the same by following the holy doctrine which \par
he taught; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\b The Presentation\b0    \i\fs20 February 2\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everliving God, we humbly beseech thee that, \par
as thy only-begotten Son was this day presented in the \par
temple, so we may be presented unto thee with pure and \par
clean hearts by the same thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord; who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 Saint Matthias\b0    \i\fs20 February 24\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, who into the place of Judas didst choose thy \par
faithful servant Matthias to be of the number of the Twelve: \par
Grant that thy Church, being delivered from false apostles, \par
may always be ordered and guided by faithful and true pastors; \par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for \par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\b Saint Joseph\b0    \i\fs20 March 19\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who from the family of thy servant David didst raise \par
up Joseph to be the guardian of thy incarnate Son and the \par
spouse of his virgin mother: Give us grace to imitate his \par
uprightness of life and his obedience to thy commands; \par
through the same thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth \par
and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever \par
and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\par
\b The Annunciation\b0    \i\fs20 March 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 We beseech thee, O Lord, pour thy grace into our hearts, that \par
we who have known the incarnation of thy Son Jesus Christ, \par
announced by an angel to the Virgin Mary, may by his cross \par
and passion be brought unto the glory of his resurrection; \par
who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy \par
Spirit, one God, now and for ever  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\par
\b Saint Mark\b0    \i\fs20 April 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who by the hand of Mark the evangelist hast\par
given to thy Church the Gospel of Jesus Christ the Son of \par
\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 God: We thank thee for this witness, and pray that we may \par
be firmly grounded in its truth; through the same Jesus Christ \par
our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy \par
Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of All Saints\i0\par
\par
\b Saint Philip and Saint James\b0    \i\fs20 May 1\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who didst give to thine apostles Philip and \par
James grace and strength to bear witness to the truth: Grant \par
that we, being mindful of their victory of faith, may glorify in \par
life and death the Name of our Lord Jesus Christ; who liveth \par
and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now \par
and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\par
Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\b The Visitation\b0    \i\fs20 May 31\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Father in heaven, by whose grace the virgin mother of thy\par
incarnate Son was blessed in bearing him, but still more blessed\par
in keeping thy word: Grant us who honor the exaltation of her\par
lowliness to follow the example of her devotion to thy will; \par
through the same Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth \par
with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\par
\b Saint Barnabas\b0    \i\fs20 June 11\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant, O God, that we may follow the example of thy \par
faithful servant Barnabas, who, seeking not his own renown \par
but the well-being of thy Church, gave generously of his life \par
and substance for the relief of the poor and the spread of the \par
Gospel; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and \par
ever.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1  \par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i Preface of Apostles\b\i0\par
\b0\f2\page\b\f4 The Nativity of Saint John the Baptist\b0    \i\fs20 June 24\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, by whose providence thy servant John the \par
Baptist was wonderfully born, and sent to prepare the way of \par
thy Son our Savior by preaching repentance: Make us so to \par
follow his doctrine and holy life, that we may truly repent \par
according to his preaching; and after his example constantly \par
speak the truth, boldly rebuke vice, and patiently suffer for \par
the truth's sake; through the same thy Son Jesus Christ our \par
Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit \par
one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Advent\i0\par
\par
\b Saint Peter and Saint Paul\b0    \i\fs20 June 29\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, whose blessed apostles Peter and Paul \par
glorified thee by their martyrdom: Grant that thy Church, \par
instructed by their teaching and example, and knit together \par
in unity by thy Spirit, may ever stand firm upon the one \par
foundation, which is Jesus Christ our Lord; who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Spirit, one God, \par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\b Independence Day\b0    \i\fs20 July 4\i0\fs24\par
\par
Lord God Almighty, in whose Name the founders of this\par
country won liberty for themselves and for us, and lit the \par
torch of freedom for nations then unborn:  Grant we beseech\par
thee, that we and all the people of this land may have grace \par
to maintain these liberties in righteousness and peace; \par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 The Collect \ldblquote For the Nation,\rdblquote  page 207, may be used instead.\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 Saint Mary Magdalene\b0    \i\fs20 July 22\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, whose blessed Son restored Mary Magdalene\par
to health of body and mind, and called her to be a witness of \par
his resurrection:  Mercifully grant that by thy grace we may \par
be healed of all our infirmities and know thee in the power of \par
his endless life; who with thee and the Holy Spirit liveth and \par
reigneth, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of All Saints\i0\par
\par
\b Saint James\b0    \i\fs20 July 25\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O gracious God, we remember before thee this day thy \par
servant and apostle James, first among the Twelve to suffer \par
martyrdom for the Name of Jesus Christ; and we pray that \par
thou wilt pour out upon the leaders of thy Church that spirit \par
of self-denying service by which alone they may have true \par
authority among thy people; through the same Jesus Christ \par
our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy \par
Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\par
Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\b The Transfiguration\b0    \i\fs20 August 6\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who on the holy mount didst reveal to chosen \par
witnesses thy well-beloved Son, wonderfully transfigured, in \par
raiment white and glistening:  Mercifully grant that we, being \par
delivered from the disquietude of this world, may by faith \par
behold the King in his beauty; who with thee, O Father, and \par
thee, O Holy Ghost, liveth and reigneth, one God, world\par
without end.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 Saint Mary the Virgin\b0    \i\fs20 August 15\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who hast taken to thyself the blessed Virgin Mary, \par
mother of thy incarnate Son:  Grant that we, who have been \par
redeemed by his blood, may share with her the glory of thine\par
eternal kingdom; through the same thy Son Jesus Christ our\par
Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the\par
Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Incarnation\i0\par
\par
\b Saint Bartholomew\b0    \i\fs20 August 24\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty and everlasting God, who didst give to thine\par
apostle Bartholomew grace truly to believe and to preach thy \par
Word:  Grant, we beseech thee, unto thy Church to love what \par
he believed and to preach what he taught; through Jesus \par
Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the \par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\b Holy Cross Day\b0    \i\fs20 September 14\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, whose Son our Savior Jesus Christ was lifted \par
high upon the cross that he might draw the whole world unto \par
himself:  Mercifully grant that we, who glory in the mystery \par
of our redemption, may have grace to take up our cross and \par
follow him; who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy \par
Spirit, one God, in glory everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Holy Week\i0\par
\par
\b Saint Matthew\b0    \i\fs20 September 21\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 We thank thee, heavenly Father, for the witness of thine\par
apostle and evangelist Matthew to the Gospel of thy Son our \par
Savior; and we pray that, after his example, we may with \par
\f2\page\f4 ready wills and hearts obey the calling of our Lord to follow \par
him; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth \par
with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.\i  Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\b Saint Michael and All Angels\b0    \i\fs20 September 29\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O everlasting God, who hast ordained and constituted the\par
ministries of angels and men in a wonderful order: Mercifully \par
grant that, as thy holy angels always serve and worship thee in \par
heaven, so by thy appointment they may help and defend us \par
on earth; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever \par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
\par
\b Saint Luke\b0    \i\fs20 October 18\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who didst inspire thy servant Luke the \par
physician to set forth in the Gospel the love and healing \par
power of thy Son:  Graciously continue in thy Church the like\par
love and power to heal, to the praise and glory of thy Name; \par
through the same thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth \par
and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one \par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of All Saints\i0\par
\par
\b Saint James of Jerusalem\b0   \i\fs20 October 23\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant, we beseech thee, O God, that after the example of thy \par
servant James the Just, brother of our Lord, thy Church may \par
give itself continually to prayer and to the reconciliation of \par
all who are at variance and enmity; through the same our \par
Lord Jesus Christ, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the \par
Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of All Saints\i0\par
\b\par
\b0\f2\page\b\f4 Saint Simon and Saint Jude\b0    \i\fs20 October 28\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, we thank thee for the glorious company of the \par
apostles, and especially on this day for Simon and Jude; and \par
we pray that, as they were faithful and zealous in their \par
mission, so we may with ardent devotion make known the \par
love and mercy of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ; who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\b All Saints\rquote  Day\b0    \i\fs20 November 1\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, who hast knit together thine elect in one \par
communion and fellowship in the mystical body of thy Son \par
Christ our Lord:  Grant us grace so to follow thy blessed \par
saints in all virtuous and godly living, that we may come to \par
those ineffable joys which thou hast prepared for those who \par
unfeignedly love thee; through the same Jesus Christ our \par
Lord, who with thee and the Holy Spirit liveth and reigneth, \par
one God, in glory everlasting.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of All Saints\par
\i0\par
\b Thanksgiving Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and gracious Father, we give thee thanks for the \par
fruits of the earth in their season and for the labors of those \par
who harvest them.  Make us, we beseech thee, faithful stewards \par
of thy great bounty, for the provision of our necessities and \par
the relief of all who are in need, to the glory of thy Name;\par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with\par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\par
\fs20 For the Prayers of the People, the Litany of Thanksgiving on page 836\par
may be used\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
\par
\f2\page\f4\fs36 The Common of Saints\fs24\par
\par
\par
\i\fs20 The festival of a saint is observed in accordance with the rules of \par
precedence set forth in the Calendar of the Church Year.\par
\par
At the discretion of the Celebrant, and as appropriate, any of the \par
following Collects, with one of the corresponding sets of Psalms and \par
Lessons, may be used\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 a) at the commemoration of a saint listed in the Calendar for which no \par
Proper is provided in this Book\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 b) at the patronal festival or commemoration of a saint not listed in \par
the Calendar.\par
\i0\fs24\par
\par
\b Of a Martyr\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, who didst give to thy servant \i N\i0 . boldness to\par
confess the Name of our Savior Jesus Christ before the rulers\par
of this world, and courage to die for this faith: Grant that we\par
may always be ready to give a reason for the hope that is in\par
us, and to suffer gladly for the sake of the same our Lord \par
Jesus Christ; who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy \par
Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, by whose grace and power thy holy martyr\par
\i N\i0 . triumphed over suffering and was faithful even unto \par
death:  Grant us, who now remember \i him\i0  with thanksgiving, \par
to be so faithful in our witness to thee in this world, that we \par
may receive with \i him\i0  the crown of life; through Jesus Christ \par
our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy \par
Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 or the following\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 Almighty and everlasting God, who didst enkindle the flame \par
of thy love in the heart of thy holy martyr \i N\i0 .: Grant to us, \par
thy humble servants, a like faith and power of love, that we \par
who rejoice in \i her\i0  triumph may profit by \i her\i0  example; \par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of a Saint\i0\par
\par
\b Of a Missionary\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, we thank thee for thy\par
servant \i N\i0 ., whom thou didst call to preach the Gospel to the \par
people of__________ (\i or\i0  to the___________ people). Raise\par
up, we beseech thee, in this and every land evangelists and \par
heralds of thy kingdom, that thy Church may proclaim the \par
unsearchable riches of our Savior Jesus Christ; who liveth \par
and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now \par
and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who willest to be glorified in thy saints, and \par
didst raise up thy servant \i N\i0 . to be a light in the world: Shine, \par
we pray thee, in our hearts, that we also in our generation \par
may show forth thy praise, who hast called us out of darkness \par
into thy marvelous light; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Pentecost\i0\par
\par
\b Of a Pastor\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O heavenly Father, Shepherd of thy people, we give thee \par
thanks for thy servant \i N\i0 ., who was faithful in the care and \par
nurture of thy flock; and we pray that, following \i his\i0  example \par
and the teaching of \i his\i0  holy life, we may by thy grace grow \par
\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 into the stature of the fullness of our Lord and Savior Jesus \par
Christ; who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy \par
Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, our heavenly Father, who didst raise up thy faithful \par
servant \i N\i0 . to be a [bishop and] pastor in thy Church and to \par
feed thy flock:  Give abundantly to all pastors the gifts of thy \par
Holy Spirit, that they may minister in thy household as true \par
servants of Christ and stewards of thy divine mysteries; \par
through the same Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the same Spirit, one God, for ever and \par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of a Saint\i0\par
\par
\b Of a Theologian and Teacher\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who by thy Holy Spirit dost give to some the word of \par
wisdom, to others the word of knowledge, and to others the \par
word of faith:  We praise thy Name for the gifts of grace \par
manifested in thy servant \i N\i0 ., and we pray that thy Church \par
may never be destitute of such gifts; through Jesus Christ our \par
Lord, who with thee and the same Spirit liveth and reigneth, \par
one God, for ever and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, who didst give to thy servant \i N\i0 . special\par
gifts of grace to understand and teach the truth as it is in\par
Christ Jesus: Grant, we beseech thee, that by this teaching we \par
may know thee, the one true God, and Jesus Christ whom \par
thou hast sent; who liveth and reigneth with thee and the \par
Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of a Saint, or of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 Of a Monastic\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, whose blessed Son became poor that we through his \par
poverty might be rich:  Deliver us, we pray thee from an \par
inordinate love of this world, that, inspired by the devotion \par
of thy servant \i N\i0 ., we may serve thee with singleness of heart, \par
and attain to the riches of the age to come; through the same\par
thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for \par
ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, by whose grace thy servant \i N\i0 ., enkindled with the \par
fire of thy love, became a burning and a shining light in thy\par
Church:  Grant that we also may be aflame with the spirit \par
of love and discipline, and may ever walk before thee as \par
children of light; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who with \par
thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, liveth and reigneth, one \par
God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of a Saint\i0\par
\par
\b Of a Saint\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, who hast compassed us about with so great \par
a cloud of witnesses: Grant that we, encouraged by the good \par
example of thy servant \i N\i0 ., may persevere in running the race \par
that is set before us, until at length, through thy mercy, we may \par
with \i him\i0  attain to thine eternal joy; through Jesus Christ, the \par
author and perfecter of our faith, who liveth and reigneth \par
with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who hast brought us near to an innumerable \par
company of angels and to the spirits of just men made \par
perfect:  Grant us during our earthly pilgrimage to abide in \par
their fellowship, and in our heavenly country to become \par
\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 partakers of their joy; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, who by thy Holy Spirit hast made us one \par
with thy saints in heaven and on earth:  Grant that in our \par
earthly pilgrimage we may ever be supported by this \par
fellowship of love and prayer, and may know ourselves \par
to be surrounded by their witness to thy power and mercy.  \par
We ask this for the sake of Jesus Christ, in whom all our \par
intercessions are acceptable through the Spirit, and who \par
liveth and reigneth for ever and ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of a Saint\i0\par
\par
\par
\par
\b\fs36 Various Occasions\b0\fs24\par
\par
\par
\i\fs20 For optional use, when desired, subject to the rules set forth in the \par
Calendar of the Church Year.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\par
\b 1. Of the Holy Trinity\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who hast revealed to thy Church thine eternal\par
Being of glorious majesty and perfect love as one God in \par
Trinity of Persons: Give us grace to continue steadfast in the \par
confession of this faith, and constant in our worship of thee, \par
Father, Son, and Holy Spirit; who livest and reignest, one \par
God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 2. Of the Holy Spirit\b0\par
\par
Almighty and most merciful God, grant, we beseech thee,\par
that by the indwelling of thy Holy Spirit we may be enlightened \par
and strengthened for thy service; through Jesus Christ our \par
Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the \par
same Spirit, one God, world without end.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Pentecost\i0\par
\par
\b 3. Of the Holy Angels\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O everlasting God, who hast ordained and constituted the\par
ministries of angels and men in a wonderful order: Mercifully \par
grant that, as thy holy angels always serve and worship thee in \par
heaven, so by thy appointment they may help and defend us \par
on earth; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever \par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
\par
\b 4. Of the Incarnation\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who didst wonderfully create, and yet more \par
wonderfully restore, the dignity of human nature: Grant\par
that we may share the divine life of him who humbled\par
himself to share our humanity, thy Son Jesus Christ; who\par
liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 5.  Of the Holy Eucharist\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 Especially suitable for Thursdays\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 God our Father, whose Son our Lord Jesus Christ in a\par
wonderful Sacrament hath left unto us a memorial of his \par
passion: Grant us so to venerate the sacred mysteries of his \par
Body and Blood, that we may ever perceive within ourselves \par
the fruit of his redemption; who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Epiphany\i0\par
\par
\b 6. Of the Holy Cross\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 Especially suitable for Fridays\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, whose beloved Son willingly endured the \par
agony and shame of the cross for our redemption: Give us \par
courage, we beseech thee, to take up our cross and follow \par
him; who liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Holy Week\i0\par
\par
\b 7. For All Baptized Christians\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 Especially suitable for Saturdays\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant, O Lord God, to all who have been baptized into the\par
death and resurrection of thy Son Jesus Christ, that, as we\par
have put away the old life of sin, so we may be renewed in\par
the spirit of our minds, and live in righteousness and true \par
holiness; through the same Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth \par
and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one \par
God, now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Baptism\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 8. For the Departed\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O eternal Lord God, who holdest all souls in life: Give, we\par
beseech thee, to thy whole Church in paradise and on earth \par
thy light and thy peace; and grant that we, following the \par
good examples of those who have served thee here and are \par
now at rest, may at the last enter with them into thine \par
unending joy; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, we remember this day before thee thy faithful \par
servant \i N\i0 .; and we pray that, having opened to \i him\i0  the gates \par
of larger life, thou wilt receive \i him\i0  more and more into thy \par
joyful service, that, with all who have faithfully served thee in \par
the past, \i he\i0  may share in the eternal victory of Jesus Christ \par
our Lord; who liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of \par
the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 Any of the Collects appointed for use at the Burial of the Dead may be \par
used instead.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 For the Prayers of the People, one of the forms appointed for the \par
Burial of the Dead may be used.\fs24\par
\par
Preface of the Commemoration of the Dead\par
\par
\fs20 The postcommunion prayer on page 482 may be used\i0 .\fs24\par
\par
\b 9. Of the Reign of Christ\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, whose will it is to restore all\par
things in thy well-beloved Son, the King of kings and Lord of \par
\f2\page\f4 lords:  Mercifully grant that the peoples of the earth, divided \par
and enslaved by sin, may be freed and brought together \par
under his most gracious rule; who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Ascension, or of Baptism\i0\par
\par
\b 10.  At Baptism\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who by our baptism into the death and \par
resurrection of thy Son Jesus Christ dost turn us from the old \par
life of sin: Grant that we, being reborn to new life in him, \par
may live in righteousness and holiness all our days; through \par
the same thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and \par
for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Baptism\i0\par
\par
\b 11. At Confirmation\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Grant, Almighty God, that we, who have been redeemed\par
from the old life of sin by our baptism into the death and \par
resurrection of thy Son Jesus Christ, may be renewed in thy \par
Holy Spirit, and live in righteousness and true holiness; \par
through the same Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and\par
reigneth with thee and the same Spirit, one God, now and\par
for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Baptism, or of Pentecost\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 12. On the Anniversary of the Dedication of a Church\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, to whose glory we celebrate the dedication\par
of this house of prayer: We give thee thanks for the fellowship\par
of those who have worshiped in this place; and we pray that \par
all who seek thee here may find thee, and be filled with thy \par
joy and peace; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 The Litany of Thanksgiving for a Church, page 578, may be used for the \par
Prayers of the People.\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Dedication of a Church\i0\par
\par
\b 13.  For a Church Convention\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting Father, who hast given the Holy\par
Spirit to abide with us for ever: Bless, we beseech thee, with \par
his grace and presence, the bishops and the other clergy and \par
the laity here (\i or\i0  now, \i or\i0  soon to be) assembled in thy Name, \par
that thy Church, being preserved in true faith and godly\par
discipline, may fulfill all the mind of him who loved it and \par
gave himself for it, thy Son Jesus Christ our Savior; who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Spirit, \par
one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Pentecost, or of the Season\i0\par
\par
\b 14.  For the Unity of the Church\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty Father, whose blessed Son before his passion \par
prayed for his disciples that they might be one, even as thou\par
and he are one: Grant that thy Church, being bound together \par
in love and obedience to thee, may be united in one body by \par
the one Spirit, that the world may believe in him whom thou \par
\par
\par
\f2\page\f4 didst send, the same thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord; who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Spirit, \par
one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Baptism, or of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
\par
\b 15.  For the Ministry (Ember Days)\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 For use on the traditional days or at other times\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 I.  For those to be ordained\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\i0\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, the giver of all good gifts, who of thy divine \par
providence hast appointed various orders in thy Church:  \par
Give thy grace, we humbly beseech thee, to all who are [now]\par
called to any office and ministry for thy people; and so fill \par
them with the truth of thy doctrine and clothe them with \par
holiness of life, that they may faithfully serve before thee, to \par
the glory of thy great Name and for the benefit of thy holy \par
Church; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Apostles\i0\par
\par
\i II.  For the choice of fit persons for the ministry\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who didst lead thy holy apostles to ordain ministers \par
in every place:  Grant that thy Church, under the guidance of \par
the Holy Spirit, may choose suitable persons for the ministry \par
of Word and Sacrament, and may uphold them in their work \par
for the extension of thy kingdom; through him who is the \par
Shepherd and Bishop of our souls, Jesus Christ our Lord, \par
who liveth and reigneth with thee and the same Spirit, one \par
God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Season\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\i\f4 III. For all Christians in their vocation\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty and everlasting God, by whose Spirit the whole\par
body of thy faithful people is governed and sanctified: \par
Receive our supplications and prayers, which we offer before\par
thee for all members of thy holy Church, that in their \par
vocation and ministry they may truly and godly serve thee; \par
through our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee, in the unity of the same Spirit, one God, \par
now and for ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Baptism, or of the Season\i0\par
\par
\b 16. For the Mission of the Church\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God, who hast made of one blood all the peoples of the \par
earth, and didst send thy blessed Son to preach peace to those\par
who are far off and to those who are near:  Grant that people \par
everywhere may seek after thee and find thee, bring the \par
nations into thy fold, pour out thy Spirit upon all flesh, and \par
hasten the coming of thy kingdom; through the same thy\par
Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee \par
and the same Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 or this\i0\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O God of all the nations of the earth: Remember the\par
multitudes who have been created in thine image but have\par
not known the redeeming work of our Savior Jesus Christ;\par
and grant that, by the prayers and labors of thy holy Church, \par
they may be brought to know and worship thee as thou hast\par
been revealed in thy Son; who liveth and reigneth with thee \par
and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Season, or of Pentecost\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 17. For the Nation\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Lord God Almighty, who hast made all peoples of the earth \par
for thy glory, to serve thee in freedom and peace: Grant to \par
the people of our country a zeal for justice and the strength \par
of forbearance, that we may use our liberty in accordance \par
with thy gracious will; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 The Collect for Independence Day may be used instead.\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of Trinity Sunday\i0\par
\par
\b 18. For Peace\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Almighty God, kindle, we beseech thee, in every heart the \par
true love of peace, and guide with thy wisdom those who \par
take counsel for the nations of the earth, that in tranquillity \par
thy dominion may increase till the earth is filled with the \par
knowledge of thy love; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Season\i0\par
\par
\b 19. For Rogation Days\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i\fs20 For use on the traditional days or at other times\fs24\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 I. For fruitful seasons\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, Lord of heaven and earth:  We humbly pray\par
that thy gracious providence may give and preserve to our \par
use the harvests of the land and of the seas, and may prosper \par
all who labor to gather them, that we, who constantly receive \par
good things from thy hand, may always give thee thanks; \par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever. \i Amen.\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\i Preface of the Season\i0\par
\i\par
\i0\f2\page\i\f4 II. For commerce and industry\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, whose Son Jesus Christ in his earthly life \par
shared our toil and hallowed our labor: Be present with \par
thy people where they work; make those who carry on \par
the industries and commerce of this land responsive to thy \par
will; and give to us all a pride in what we do, and a just \par
return for our labor; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee, in the unity of the Holy Spirit, \par
one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Season\i0\par
\par
\i III. For stewardship of creation\i0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O merciful Creator, whose hand is open wide to satisfy the \par
needs of every living creature: Make us, we beseech thee,\par
ever thankful for thy loving providence; and grant that we, \par
remembering the account that we must one day give, may be \par
faithful stewards of thy bounty; through Jesus Christ our \par
Lord, who with thee and the Holy Spirit liveth and reigneth, \par
one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Season\par
\i0\par
\b 20. For the Sick\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Heavenly Father, giver of life and health: Comfort and \par
relieve thy sick servants, and give thy power of healing to \par
those who minister to their needs, that those (\i or N., or NN.) \i0\par
for whom our prayers are offered may be strengthened in\par
\i their\i0  weakness and have confidence in thy loving care; \par
through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with \par
thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Season\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1\fs20 The postcommunion prayer on page 457 may be used.\i0\fs24\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 21. For Social Justice\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who hast created us in thine own image:  \par
Grant us grace fearlessly to contend against evil and to make \par
no peace with oppression; and, that we may reverently use \par
our freedom, help us to employ it in the maintenance of \par
justice in our communities and among the nations, to the \par
glory of thy holy Name; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who \par
liveth and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, \par
now and for ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Season\i0\par
\par
\b 22. For Social Service\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 O Lord our heavenly Father, whose blessed Son came not to \par
be ministered unto but to minister: Bless, we beseech thee, all\par
who, following in his steps, give themselves to the service of\par
others; that with wisdom, patience, and courage, they may\par
minister in his name to the suffering, the friendless, and the\par
needy; for the love of him who laid down his life for us, the same thy Son our Savior Jesus Christ, who liveth and reigneth \par
with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \par
\i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Season\i0\par
\par
\b 23. For Education\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, the fountain of all wisdom: Enlighten by thy \par
Holy Spirit those who teach and those who learn, that, \par
rejoicing in the knowledge of thy truth, they may worship \par
thee and serve thee from generation to generation; through \par
Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and reigneth with thee and \par
the same Spirit, one God, for ever and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Season\i0\par
\par
\par
\f2\page\b\f4 24. For Vocation in Daily Work\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God our heavenly Father, who declarest thy glory \par
and showest forth thy handiwork in the heavens and in the \par
earth:  Deliver us, we beseech thee, in our several occupations \par
from the service of self alone, that we may do the work \par
which thou givest us to do, in truth and beauty and for the \par
common good; for the sake of him who came among us as \par
one that serveth, thy Son Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth \par
and reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever \par
and ever.  \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Season\par
\i0\par
\b 25. For Labor Day\b0\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Almighty God, who hast so linked our lives one with another \par
that all we do affects, for good or ill, all other lives:  So guide \par
us in the work we do, that we may do it not for self alone, but \par
for the common good; and, as we seek a proper return for\par
our own labor, make us mindful of the rightful aspirations of \par
other workers, and arouse our concern for those who are out\par
of work; through Jesus Christ our Lord, who liveth and \par
reigneth with thee and the Holy Spirit, one God, for ever and \par
ever. \i Amen.\par
\pard\sl120\slmult1\par
\pard\sl216\slmult1 Preface of the Season\i0\par
\par
}
